From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:44:58 +0300
Subject: nv30: submit when the GPU caught up and a share of a frame is queued
 (PS3, NV30_PS3_KICK_AUTO)

Without relocations (0019) a context submits only when its push buffer fills, on a flush or
for a query, so a frame reaches the GPU in one piece at SwapBuffers and the GPU idles while
the CPU builds it. 0026's submission every N draws brings the overlap back where draws are
big (ps3.282, fps: Armagetron 50 -> 60.5 at N=100, OpenArena 51.3 -> 53.1, ClassiCube
48.3 -> 48.9) but costs where they are tiny and many (X-Moto 47.5 -> 43.0): each submission is an ioctl, the
kernel's buffer list and fences, and every bound buffer referenced again, and X-Moto's
immediate-mode draws made dozens of them per frame. A draw count is the wrong measure.

NV30_PS3_KICK_AUTO (on by default on the PS3; =0 restores ps3.282's behaviour) submits at
the start of a draw only when both hold, checked without an ioctl:
 - the work queued since the last submission is at least NV30_PS3_KICK_MIN_BYTES (16384)
   and at least 1/NV30_PS3_KICK_SPLIT (4) of the words the last frame queued (frames end at
   flushes with PIPE_FLUSH_END_OF_FRAME), so a frame is cut into at most about that many
   parts whatever its draw count: a few extra submissions per frame, never dozens;
 - the GPU has finished everything submitted before: the fence notifier (a plain read of
   mapped memory, nv30_screen_fence_update) has caught up with the last fence emitted. While
   the GPU still works on earlier work a submission adds no overlap, only its cost, and the
   check comes again at the next draw.
NV30_PS3_KICK_DRAWS=N still overrides it (and turns it off). All read once at screen
creation.

Same command stream, cut into more submissions. What would confirm it on the PS3 (HUD fps,
against ps3.282's defaults / kick100): Armagetron near kick100's 60.5 (defaults 50),
X-Moto at least the defaults' 47.5 (kick100: 43.0), OpenArena near kick100's 53.1 (51.3),
ClassiCube at least its defaults' 48.3 (kick100: 48.9). If X-Moto still loses, try NV30_PS3_KICK_SPLIT=2 or a
larger NV30_PS3_KICK_MIN_BYTES; if Armagetron gains less than kick100, NV30_PS3_KICK_SPLIT=8.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.c
@@ -42,6 +42,14 @@ nv30_context_kick_notify(struct nouveau_pushbuf *push)
    struct nouveau_pushbuf_priv *p = push->user_priv;
    struct nouveau_screen *screen = p->screen;
 
+   /* NV30_PS3_KICK_AUTO: this submission's words count towards the frame's size */
+   struct nv30_context *nv30 = nv30_context(&p->context->pipe);
+   if (nv30->kick_mark) {
+      if (push->cur >= nv30->kick_mark && push->cur - nv30->kick_mark <= (1 << 20))
+         nv30->frame_words += push->cur - nv30->kick_mark;
+      nv30->kick_mark = NULL;
+   }
+
    if (!_nouveau_fence_next(p->context))
       return false;
    _nouveau_fence_update(screen, true);
@@ -86,6 +94,10 @@ nv30_context_flush(struct pipe_context *pipe, struct pipe_fence_handle **fence,
       return;
    PUSH_KICK(push);
    nv30->draws_since_kick = 0;
+   if (flags & PIPE_FLUSH_END_OF_FRAME) {
+      nv30->frame_words_last = nv30->frame_words;
+      nv30->frame_words = 0;
+   }
 
    /* another context may sample what this one rendered or copied */
    p_atomic_inc(&nv30->screen->tex_gen);
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
@@ -68,6 +68,12 @@ struct nv30_context {
    /* draws since the last submission of this context (NV30_PS3_KICK_DRAWS) */
    unsigned draws_since_kick;
 
+   /* NV30_PS3_KICK_AUTO: the push buffer position at the first draw after the last
+    * submission (NULL: none since), and the words queued in this frame and the last one */
+   uint32_t *kick_mark;
+   unsigned frame_words;
+   unsigned frame_words_last;
+
    /* PS3: bytes of texture upload staging (GART) whose copies may still be pending */
    unsigned staging_inflight;
 
